    {
      "page_idx": 1,
      "blocks": [
        {
          "type": "header",
          "bbox": [
            0.885,
            0.021,
            0.961,
            0.039
          ],
          "content": "9/27/26"
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph_title",
          "bbox": [
            0.202,
            0.124,
            0.375,
            0.143
          ],
          "level": 2,
          "content": "Dynamic Bug Search"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.115,
            0.154,
            0.428,
            0.171
          ],
          "content": "• Start with a small number of print statement"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.134,
            0.172,
            0.375,
            0.188
          ],
          "content": "§ Put them in the area you think error is"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.133,
            0.188,
            0.407,
            0.205
          ],
          "content": "§ Leave large sections of code between prints"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.116,
            0.205,
            0.429,
            0.222
          ],
          "content": "• Find the first print statement that is “wrong”"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.132,
            0.223,
            0.424,
            0.24
          ],
          "content": "§ Error is must be before it (and after last print?)"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.134,
            0.239,
            0.375,
            0.255
          ],
          "content": "§ Add more print statements in this area"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.133,
            0.255,
            0.327,
            0.271
          ],
          "content": "§ Repeat this process as needed"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.116,
            0.272,
            0.434,
            0.29
          ],
          "content": "• Problem is when cannot find anything wrong"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.132,
            0.29,
            0.425,
            0.307
          ],
          "content": "§ Pick an area that was hard and add more prints"
        },
        {
          "type": "page_number",
          "bbox": [
            0.526,
            0.332,
            0.539,
            0.345
          ],
          "content": "8"
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph_title",
          "bbox": [
            0.605,
            0.124,
            0.818,
            0.143
          ],
          "level": 2,
          "content": "Aiding the Search Process"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.539,
            0.154,
            0.776,
            0.173
          ],
          "content": "• In practice, searching is hard"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.556,
            0.174,
            0.878,
            0.192
          ],
          "content": "§ Errors can go a long time until we catch them"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.556,
            0.193,
            0.843,
            0.211
          ],
          "content": "§ Errors often seen by user, not developer"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.54,
            0.212,
            0.842,
            0.231
          ],
          "content": "• Would be easier if errors just crashed"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.556,
            0.232,
            0.805,
            0.25
          ],
          "content": "§ A crash always gives a stack trace"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.556,
            0.251,
            0.807,
            0.27
          ],
          "content": "§ The user can just email that to you"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.539,
            0.27,
            0.82,
            0.289
          ],
          "content": "• We do this with **assert statements**"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.551,
            0.29,
            0.844,
            0.309
          ],
          "content": "§ Crash the program when an error is seen"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.675,
            0.307,
            0.748,
            0.319
          ],
          "content": "Asserts & Debugging"
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph_title",
          "bbox": [
            0.215,
            0.406,
            0.363,
            0.423
          ],
          "level": 2,
          "content": "Assert Statements"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.116,
            0.435,
            0.308,
            0.452
          ],
          "content": "• **Form 1:** assert &lt;boolean&gt;"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.133,
            0.452,
            0.338,
            0.469
          ],
          "content": "§ Does nothing if boolean is True"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.133,
            0.47,
            0.356,
            0.485
          ],
          "content": "§ Creates an error is boolean is False"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.115,
            0.486,
            0.368,
            0.503
          ],
          "content": "• **Form 2:** assert &lt;boolean&gt;, &lt;string&gt;"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.134,
            0.505,
            0.288,
            0.52
          ],
          "content": "§ Very much like form 2"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.133,
            0.52,
            0.369,
            0.536
          ],
          "content": "§ But error message includes the string"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.116,
            0.538,
            0.359,
            0.555
          ],
          "content": "• Statement to **verify a fact is true**"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.133,
            0.555,
            0.392,
            0.571
          ],
          "content": "§ Similar to assert\\_equals used in unit tests"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.134,
            0.571,
            0.415,
            0.589
          ],
          "content": "§ But more versatile with complete **stack trace**"
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph_title",
          "bbox": [
            0.58,
            0.405,
            0.842,
            0.425
          ],
          "level": 2,
          "content": "Example: Anglicizing an Integer"
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph_title",
          "bbox": [
            0.553,
            0.438,
            0.651,
            0.455
          ],
          "level": 2,
          "content": "def anglicize(n):"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.566,
            0.457,
            0.779,
            0.474
          ],
          "content": "\"\"\"Returns: the anglicization of int n."
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.566,
            0.476,
            0.816,
            0.493
          ],
          "content": "Precondition: n an int, 0 < n < 1,000,000\"\"\""
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.566,
            0.494,
            0.822,
            0.51
          ],
          "content": "assert <u>type(n) == int, repr(n)</u>+' is not an int'"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.567,
            0.51,
            0.884,
            0.526
          ],
          "content": "assert <u>0 < n and n < 1000000</u>, <u>repr(n)+' is out of range'</u>"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.568,
            0.526,
            0.726,
            0.542
          ],
          "content": "\\# Implement method here…"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.575,
            0.545,
            0.661,
            0.56
          ],
          "content": "Check (part of)"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.574,
            0.56,
            0.662,
            0.575
          ],
          "content": "the precondition"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.744,
            0.546,
            0.824,
            0.56
          ],
          "content": "Error message"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.744,
            0.56,
            0.823,
            0.574
          ],
          "content": "when violated"
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph_title",
          "bbox": [
            0.148,
            0.686,
            0.428,
            0.705
          ],
          "level": 2,
          "content": "Enforcing Preconditions is Tricky!"
        },
        {
          "type": "page_number",
          "bbox": [
            0.526,
            0.614,
            0.548,
            0.627
          ],
          "content": "10"
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph_title",
          "bbox": [
            0.13,
            0.719,
            0.259,
            0.735
          ],
          "level": 2,
          "content": "def lookup\\_netid(nid):"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.142,
            0.738,
            0.389,
            0.754
          ],
          "content": "\"\"\"Returns: name of student with netid nid."
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.142,
            0.757,
            0.409,
            0.773
          ],
          "content": "Precondition: nid is a string, which consists of"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.144,
            0.771,
            0.319,
            0.786
          ],
          "content": "2 or 3 letters and a number\"\"\""
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.143,
            0.787,
            0.438,
            0.804
          ],
          "content": "assert type(nid) == str, repr(nid) + ' is not a string'"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.144,
            0.803,
            0.443,
            0.82
          ],
          "content": "assert nid.isalnum(), repr(nid)+' is not letters/digits"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.151,
            0.832,
            0.285,
            0.847
          ],
          "content": "Returns True if s contains"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.344,
            0.833,
            0.427,
            0.847
          ],
          "content": "Does this catch"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.159,
            0.847,
            0.277,
            0.861
          ],
          "content": "only letters, numbers."
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.345,
            0.847,
            0.425,
            0.861
          ],
          "content": "all violations?"
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph_title",
          "bbox": [
            0.548,
            0.686,
            0.874,
            0.705
          ],
          "level": 2,
          "content": "Using Function to Enforce Preconditions"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.539,
            0.719,
            0.781,
            0.734
          ],
          "content": "def exchange(curr\\_from, curr\\_to, amt\\_from):"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.565,
            0.736,
            0.778,
            0.752
          ],
          "content": "\"\"\"Returns: amount of curr\\_to received."
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.565,
            0.753,
            0.823,
            0.768
          ],
          "content": "Precondition: curr\\_from is a valid currency code"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.565,
            0.767,
            0.81,
            0.781
          ],
          "content": "Precondition: curr\\_to is a valid currency code"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.565,
            0.779,
            0.758,
            0.793
          ],
          "content": "Precondition: amt\\_from is a float\"\"\""
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.562,
            0.793,
            0.803,
            0.808
          ],
          "content": "assert **??????**, repr(curr\\_from) + ' not valid"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.562,
            0.809,
            0.803,
            0.824
          ],
          "content": "assert **??????**, repr(curr\\_from) + ' not valid'"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.562,
            0.824,
            0.878,
            0.84
          ],
          "content": "assert type(amt\\_from)==float, repr(amt\\_from)+' not a float"
        },
        {
          "type": "page_number",
          "bbox": [
            0.103,
